TIP:  If you consult your Leslie Knope “Pre-Planning Binder for the Passing of Li’l Sebastian” you’ll see on page 246 the use of the (Dsus) chord which is just (D) with your pinky added to the 1st string/3rd fret.  Similarly, on page 412 you’ll see the (Asus) in which you hold (A) and either slide your bottom finger or add your pinky to the 2nd string/3rd fret.  All that’s missing is a Duke Silver saxophone solo. 
 

